{
  "corpus": "vutex-math-gate",
  "version": 1,
  "source": "TeXbook chapter 17 math examples and the KaTeX supported-functions list, curated from VuTeX's acceptance formulas",
  "notes": "Every layout case must clear the semantic and geometry gate in `vutex-render-svg/tests/corpus_invariants.rs`. `style` is the style the case is meant to exercise: `display` lays out with the display pipeline, `text` and `script` use the inline pipeline (`script` carries an explicit style command in `src`). `body` names the content a stretched delimiter wraps so the delimiter extent can be compared against it. `expected` is `layout` or `error`, and `diagnostics` records whether a diagnostic is expected to reach the user (a parse error does).",
